   "title": "How this works",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 0b \u00b7 The shots\nGemma 4 12B (8-bit) turns the story **beats** (written by 11 \u00b7 story writer) into shots: the beat each shot tells, what the camera sees, the shot size, the camera move, the length, the sound, and whether the lead is in it.\n\n**mode**: *board* writes one shot for each beat in `write_beats` (around the kept shots in `shots`), or `count` shots that start or continue the film; *next* writes the shot after `shots`; *rewrite* writes shot `index` again. Sizes and moves are snapped to the studio's presets. Each shot is then drawn by **14 \u00b7 storyboard**.\n\nAI mode: Normal uses Gemma 4 12B at 8-bit; Fast uses E4B. Change the Open Cinema Writer mode widget. Image and video models stay the same. Cast-review findings retain the saved candidate; inspect it before using it downstream."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
